@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title What ChatHealthy.ai trusts at each step, and what is allowed to cross

rectangle "The person's browser and the static pages we own" #fff1f2 {
  component "ClientRouter.js\nthe only file in Website/ that calls a service" as CR
  artifact "sessionStorage\nthe signed session token" as SS
  component "static pages we own\nwitnessed by an onload event, no session" as STATIC
  CR -- SS
}

cloud "Third parties\nOAuth and other callbacks" as TP

rectangle "The entrance — SharedServices, the only host that accepts external traffic" #fef9c3 {
  component "Gate\na dumb web-server facade — the only\ncomponent that knows transport exists.\nCollects the session token, the HTTP head,\nand the GET/POST parameters, passes them\nto the UniversalNavigator, streams the one\nanswer back. Verifies nothing itself." as GATE
  component "UniversalNavigator (the main)\ntriage / route / render-ledger / merge —\nthe only node that accepts external traffic" as UN
  component "UtteranceManager\ndecides whether an utterance is sufficient to dispatch to one or more tools, and dispatches if so.\ncapability: RequestUsersRefinement — the single surface that asks the user.\nRequestUsersRefinement() — the UM's own LLM authors the question when no route or a missing slot is found.\nRequestUsersRefinement(question) — a dispatched tool authored the question and the UM delivers it." as UM
  GATE --> UN
  UN --> UM
}

rectangle "Server to server — tool-to-tool only, proven by our own signature" #ecfeff {
  component "FindCare container\nGate facade + UniversalNavigatorProxy + tools" as FC
  component "EvaluateCare container\nGate facade + UniversalNavigatorProxy + tools" as EC
  artifact "CERTS_DIR = /tmp/ch_certs\nshared.crt, findcare.crt,\nevalcare.crt, ca.crt\ndecoded at startup from Space secrets" as CERTS
  FC .. CERTS
  EC .. CERTS
}

rectangle "The data region — reached only with a certificate" #dcfce7 {
  component "ChatHealthyMongoUtilities\ngetConnection(identity, cluster)" as MU
  database "MongoDB (Atlas) ChatHealthyFrontEnd\nPublicHealthData (served, version-bound),\nProprietaryData, ChatHealthyConfig\n(the live registry document), Debug" as ATF
  database "MongoDB (Atlas) Session\nthe Session collection" as SESS
  database "MongoDB (Atlas) Registered Users\nthe Registered Users collection" as RU
  database "MongoDB (Atlas) ChatHealthyDataPipelines\nPipelinePublicHealthData, staging generations,\npipelineAdmin" as ATP
  MU --> ATF
  MU --> SESS
  MU --> RU
  MU --> ATP
}

rectangle "Other identities that reach MongoDB — each holds its own certificate" #dcfce7 {
  component "the operator\nsigned in via Google OAuth" as OP
  component "the entitlements API\nthe rights the operator toggles" as ENT
  component "the agent — claudeCodeAgent" as AGENT
}

cloud "Azure Key Vault\nkv-chpipeline-dev" as KV

cloud "Model vendors — three live\nOpenAI, Anthropic, Google" as LLM

cloud "Platform liveness probe\n(Azure / Hugging Face)" as PLAT

CR --> GATE : the signed session token (client_sessioned).\nProof is a session_token.\nOrigins restricted by CORS to\nlocalhost and *.chathealthy.ai
STATIC --> GATE : a page name only (static_witness).\nProof method is none — it logs, decides nothing
TP --> GATE : a credential we keep (third_party_callback).\nProof is an api_key named in the vault

UN --> FC : we sign the dispatch out (tool_to_tool);\nthe reply returns as an internal_callback,\nverified by our_signature
UN --> EC : we sign the dispatch out (tool_to_tool);\nthe reply returns as an internal_callback,\nverified by our_signature

UN --> MU : the app
FC --> MU : the app
EC --> MU : the app
OP --> MU : operator via Google OAuth
ENT --> MU : the entitlements API
AGENT --> MU : the agent

MU --> KV : an Azure token issued to this identity alone,\nexchanged for that identity's cert and key

PLAT --> GATE : GET /health — no session token, no proof;\nanswered from Mongo. OPEN: is a platform's\nliveness probe the firm's traffic at all? (N31)

UM --> LLM : typed text + recent conversation crosses out
FC --> LLM
EC --> LLM

note right of UN
  Proof-checking and session security moved here off the gate.
  The UniversalNavigator proves every arrival by the route's
  declared proof, establishes the session once, drives the
  route from the registry map, keeps the render ledger, merges
  every returning answer serially, and is the client that logs
  every downstream failure. It holds no data: the map is the
  registry, the parameters ride the passed document, the
  sessions and the ledger are repository rows. Satellites carry
  tool-to-tool traffic only and trust our signature, so the
  session is never re-litigated per hop.
end note

note bottom of ATF
  The navigation map is one Mongo document per build per
  environment; exactly one is live per environment. Writable by
  the deploying identity alone; every runtime identity reads it.
  The UniversalNavigator reads its environment's live document
  at startup and hands each proxy its need-to-know slice.
end note

note bottom of CERTS
  Hugging Face Spaces cannot bind-mount a cert
  directory, so the deploy stores each PEM as a
  Space secret and startup writes them to disk.
end note

note bottom of MU
  There is no connection string and no password.
  The certificate is the credential: Atlas matches
  its subject DN to a $external user and applies
  that user's role, so an identity with no
  certificate simply cannot connect.
end note

note right of KV
  A host holds the Azure credential only for the
  identities it is entitled to act as. One credential
  serving every identity would let the workstation
  read the front end's certificate, and the front
  end's read the pipeline's.
end note

note top of ATF
  Data is versioned in real time, NOT environment-segregated:
  the served generation is a record value in
  ChatHealthyConfig.DBVersions, resolved at connect. There are
  no dev_/qa_/prod_ databases; legacy env-prefixed FindCare DBs
  are the residue of the pre-versioning era and are pruning
  candidates. Migration PipelinePublicHealthData -> PublicHealthData
  is name-preserving and human-released. (N11 / C4.)
end note

@enduml
